  "summary": "Mistune: Path Traversal and XSS in Include directive",
  "details": "The Include directive in `src/mistune/directives/include.py` does not validate that the resolved file path stays within the source directory, allowing path traversal via `../` sequences to read arbitrary files.\n\nAdditionally, error messages and included file contents are rendered without HTML escaping, leading to XSS even when `escape=True`.\n\nAffected functions:\n- Path resolution (lines 27-31)\n- `block_error()` in html.py (line 140)\n- `render_html_include()` (line 72)\n\nThe Include plugin must be explicitly enabled via the plugins parameter.",
